				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάκαρ</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>, <i>one blessed</i>, i.e. <i>dead</i>, esp. of one
				<i>lately dead</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				633
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				488.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				1032
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				447.1
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>: freq. in late writers, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.120b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.113e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ μ. σου πατήρ</span> your
				<i>late</i> father, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMeretr.</u>
				6.1
			</span></i>, etc.:—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾰκᾰρ-ῖτις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				2.70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				6.55
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ μ. μου γυνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Philops.</u>
					27
				</span></i>
			. </div>
